  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Background: This bug appears to have existed since the inception of API-A Lite.  I discovered it while working on refactoring item 1814192 (Constants for namespace/schema uris/locs).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In API-A Lite, many of the XML responses are not namespace-qualified.  It appears the intent was to have all of these responses exist in the \"/definitions/1/0/api/access\" namespace, but the way the XML is written doesn't do that.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For example, objectProfile's root element is (non-namespace-qualified) \"objectProfile\", and contains the following namespace/xsd-related attributes: \"xmlns:xsi\", \"xsi:schemaLocation\".  What's missing is an xmlns attribute that declares the namespace of the current element (and children) to be \"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.fedora.info/definitions/1/0/access/"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.fedora.info/definitions/1/0/access/",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
