  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>Background: This bug appears to have existed since the inception of API-A Lite.  I discovered it while working on refactoring item 1814192 (Constants for namespace/schema uris/locs).</p>\n\n<p>In API-A Lite, many of the XML responses are not namespace-qualified.  It appears the intent was to have all of these responses exist in the \"/definitions/1/0/api/access\" namespace, but the way the XML is written doesn't do that.</p>\n\n<p>For example, objectProfile's root element is (non-namespace-qualified) \"objectProfile\", and contains the following namespace/xsd-related attributes: \"xmlns:xsi\", \"xsi:schemaLocation\".  What's missing is an xmlns attribute that declares the namespace of the current element (and children) to be \"http://www.fedora.info/definitions/1/0/access/\"</p>",
